Third-party JSON-LD @context documents, vendored so Mere can resolve standard
vocabularies offline (no network fetch during ingest). Bundled verbatim, not
modified. Each is a separately-licensed data asset; the surrounding crate is
MPL-2.0 and is unaffected (aggregation, not adaptation).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
schema.org.context.jsonld

  Source:  https://schema.org/docs/jsonldcontext.json
  © schema.org and contributors.
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 (CC BY-SA 3.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

  Used to expand documents that reference `"@context": "https://schema.org/"`
  (and the http:// variant) offline. The schema.org context's `@vocab` is
  `http://schema.org/`, so Mere normalizes schema.org IRIs to their https form
  on ingest.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
activitystreams.context.jsonld

  Source:  https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams
  © W3C and contributors.
  License: W3C Software and Document Notice and License
           https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license/

  The normative ActivityStreams 2.0 / ActivityPub context. Used to expand
  documents that reference `"@context": "https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams"`
  offline (the fediverse).
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dublin-core.context.jsonld

  Authored by the Mere project (MPL-2.0, same as this crate — not a third-party
  asset). A small convenience context mapping the `dc:` / `dcterms:` prefixes
  and common Dublin Core terms to their IRIs, for the rare document that
  references a remote Dublin Core context. Dublin Core term recognition
  (`dcterms:title` -> title, etc.) does not depend on this file.
